        <mxCell id="summary" value="PATTERN B SUMMARY: ETL engine-side transform. Raw Parquet read from S3 by AWS Glue (serverless Spark). Cleaning, unioning, schema reconciliation, and partitioning happen outside the warehouse, producing a conformed Parquet zone in a team-owned S3 prefix. Conformed data loaded into Snowflake AMO_SILVER via external stage + COPY INTO. dbt Core builds Gold mart models for joins, aggregations, and year-over-year analysis. Broader skill demonstration than Pattern A: shows DataFrame engines, distributed processing, file formats, and partitioning. Keeps heavy row-level cleaning off Snowflake credits." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=9;fontColor=#444444;spacingLeft=5;spacingRight=5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="780" width="1540" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
